<title>USA: SF Fed's Parry surprised, unphazed by labor data.</title>
<headline>SF Fed's Parry surprised, unphazed by labor data.</headline>
<dateline>LOS ANGELES 1997-08-01</dateline>
<text>
<p>The U.S. July employment report was  somewhat surprising, but still not enough to change the underlying  trend of the current economic scenario in the country, said the president  of the Federal Reserve Bank of San Francisco.</p>
<p>&quot;Those (unemployment) numbers were a bit of a surprise and (it was)  quite impressive that the unemployment rate dropped,&quot; Robert Parry,  the president of the San Francisco Fed told a panel of economists  here on Friday.</p>
</text>
